fix(seo): restore 528 missing pages and stop linking through redirects

Three defects were invisible in local builds and only surfaced when the
deployed site was probed path by path. Local build output being correct does
not mean production behaviour is correct.

1) 528 component pages (10% of the catalogue) never existed in production.

   `repos/` is the ~370 MB set of upstream clones and is gitignored, so it is
   absent from Cloudflare's build environment. But generate-previews.mjs and
   augment-heavy-demos.mjs read it AT BUILD TIME to compile the React previews:

     buildAnimataGeneratedIds()  -> repos/animata/animata
     buildEldoraGeneratedIds()   -> repos/eldoraui/...
     buildZeldaGeneratedIds()    -> repos/zelda-hyrule-ui/packages/...
     buildThreeUIGeneratedIds()  -> repos/threeui
     buildReactBitsVideoMap()    -> repos/react-bits/public/assets/video

   Each starts with `if (!fs.existsSync(...)) return {}`, so without the clones
   those previews never reach `ready`, and the page generator only emits pages
   for `ready` entries. Result: animata 198/203, react-bits 133/269, eldoraui
   92/160, zelda 84/93 and threeui 21/93 pages silently dropped -- while
   uiverse/animejs (HTML iframe previews, no repo dependency) were unaffected.

   Both scripts now skip entirely when `repos/` is missing and keep the
   committed artefacts, instead of degrading to a subset. Verified by hiding
   `repos/` and running a full build: 5,047 pages / 5,111 URLs, identical to
   local, with the data files' checksums unchanged.

2) Every canonical and sitemap URL pointed at a redirect.

   Cloudflare serves `<slug>/index.html` at `<slug>/` and 308s the slash-less
   form (measured: /components/at-faq -> 308 -> /components/at-faq/ -> 200).
   The generated canonical and sitemap both used the slash-less form, so all
   5,111 URLs paid a redirect and every canonical named a redirect target.
   Added slugPath()/slugUrl() and converted 29 call sites: canonicals, JSON-LD
   urls, the sitemap, and every internal link including the breadcrumb objects
   (`{ label, href: '/components' }`), which the first pass missed because they
   are not HTML literals.

3) `/components` and `/showcases` were swallowed by a redirect to the home view.

   The `_redirects` 200-rewrite for those paths does not take effect in
   production; both paths answered 308 -> `/`, so deep links and hard reloads
   landed on the wrong view. The build now emits real `components/index.html`
   and `showcases/index.html` shells with per-view metadata baked into static
   HTML, which also makes those titles readable without JS. The ineffective
   rewrites are removed; `/official` -> `/` 301 is kept.

verify-seo-pages.mjs grows two regression guards: fail on any internal link
that targets a directory without a trailing slash, and on any slash-less
sitemap URL. Both are at 0.

Full record: docs/SEO_TIER2_DESIGN.md sections 14 and 15.
